wolf3d @PROJECT_VERSION@ - shared engine library
=====================================================

This is the platform-neutral Wolf3D engine library distribution. It
contains the shared engine, its public C99 header, the replaceable Nuked-OPL3
shared library, and the applicable license and provenance files.

A host must populate wolf3d_platform_api_t with its video, input, timing, error,
and PCM callbacks, call wolf3d_SetPlatform(), and then call
wolf3d_Create(), wolf3d_Run(), and wolf3d_Shutdown(). See
docs/porting-guide.md in the source distribution and the headless and Win32
hosts for complete examples.

Windows distributions also include wolf3d.lib, the import library used
to link a host against wolf3d.dll. On ELF systems the corresponding
runtime artifact is libwolf3d.so.

Official Windows packages embed the MSVC runtime and do not require the Visual
C++ Redistributable. Custom builds made with WG_STATIC_MSVC_RUNTIME=OFF use the
dynamic MSVC runtime and require the matching Redistributable.

Nuked-OPL3 is licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later and intentionally remains a
separate, replaceable shared library. See COPYING.Nuked-OPL3.txt and
THIRD_PARTY.md.
